        "description": "Runs harness/setup.mjs with --action mcp-inspect, mcp-preview, mcp-register or mcp-unregister for the AI apps named in client (a comma-separated list of claude-code, codex, gemini-cli, cursor). mcp-inspect and mcp-preview write nothing: they answer each app's config file path, whether a Trillion entry is there now, and a review_hash for the exact change. mcp-register writes the entry only when given that review_hash as reviewed, so the person sees the change before it is made; mcp-unregister takes it out. Claude Code and Codex use the bridge the Trillion Mac app installs, which keeps the account key in Keychain; an entry here does not by itself sign the app in (each result's sign_in says how). Exit 0 means every app was handled, 2 means one was blocked or has a custom entry, 1 means the request was wrong (standard error says what to change).",
